        "The festival year adds its own rhythm. Sarhul, the spring festival of the district's Adivasi communities, comes around March or April; Karma follows near the end of the rains; Christmas is a major occasion in a Christian-majority district; Dussehra and Diwali arrive in the autumn. Winter brings the Magh Mela at Ram Rekha Dham, and a Kartik Purnima fair follows. Tutors place lessons around those dates, not on top of them.",
        "For a Diploma student the school year, which begins in April, unfolds in a predictable order: Class 11 internals, Internal Assessment drafts in the first half of Class 12, predicted grades sent to universities around the turn of the year, mock exams in February or March, and the May papers after that. Where a school uses the November session, the whole chain shifts by about six months.",
