        "Subject choice follows ambition. A student who may take Maths AA or Physics HL later is well served by Extended Mathematics with Additional Mathematics and the three sciences taught separately. A student leaning towards Economics or Business should still keep Mathematics at Extended, perhaps balancing the load with Business Studies and English. Hindi as a second language is a dependable subject for a child who already speaks it at home.",
        "Cambridge and Edexcel differ more than the shared label suggests. Papers are built differently, mark schemes follow different conventions, and Edexcel's tiering has no direct Cambridge equivalent. A tutor therefore works from the board's own past papers and examiner reports, which are the real syllabus in practice. A boarding student should confirm early which board and which codes the school has entered them for.",
