  tutorsIntro:
    "IB and IGCSE tutors in Simdega, through IB Gram, cover the IB continuum and both IGCSE boards. The match is made on syllabus, level and exam session, and the lesson is always delivered online.",

  faqs: [
    { question: "How do I find an IB tutor in Simdega?", answer: "Share the programme, subject, level and exam session and we propose tutors who teach that exact course online. Because no IB school could be confirmed in Simdega or Ranchi, the shortlist ignores geography and looks at recent teaching of the syllabus, availability on IST evenings or weekends and fit with your child's pace. A free trial lesson comes before any decision, and a poor match is replaced." },
    { question: "Do you offer IGCSE home tuition in Simdega for Cambridge and Edexcel?", answer: "Yes, as online home tuition: the student sits at home and the lesson runs over video. Cambridge students are matched by subject code and tier, for example 0580 Extended Mathematics or 0620 Chemistry, and Edexcel students by specification and Foundation or Higher tier, with each board's own past papers and mark schemes used throughout. No tutor travels to a house in Simdega." },
    { question: "Do your tutors visit homes in Simdega, Kolebira or Biru?", answer: "No. Home visits run only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR, and in Simdega, Kolebira, Biru or anywhere else in Jharkhand the lesson is live, online and one-to-one. A shared whiteboard and screen-shared past papers do the job that a table and notebook would do in a room, and the student stays at home throughout." },
    { question: "What does an IB or IGCSE tutor cost in Simdega?", answer: "The rate is set for the match, written down and confirmed before your trial, and it depends on programme, subject, level, session length and the tutor's experience. IB Gram does not publish a price list, because an HL Chemistry tutor and an IGCSE Core Mathematics tutor are not interchangeable. There is no travel cost, since nothing happens in person, and no lock-in once lessons begin." },
    { question: "Which schools near Simdega offer the IB or IGCSE?", answer: "None that we could confirm in Simdega or Ranchi. Directory listings show KIIT International School in Bhubaneswar with CBSE, IGCSE and the IB Diploma, and in Kolkata Calcutta International School, RP Goenka International School and The Heritage School, each with IB or IGCSE options. These are boarding or relocation decisions, not daily journeys, and IB Gram does not arrange admissions at any of them." },
    { question: "Is there a free trial lesson before I commit?", answer: "Yes, and it always comes first. Your child works on a real topic from their own syllabus with the proposed tutor, live and free of charge, and a short written plan follows. The trial also shows what a profile cannot: how the tutor explains, whether your child asks questions freely and whether video and audio hold up on your connection. You can continue, ask for changes or request another tutor, with nothing owed." },
    { question: "Can a tutor help with IB Internal Assessments in Simdega?", answer: "A tutor can coach the process but never writes any part of an assessed piece. That means helping a student choose a workable research question, explaining what each criterion rewards, discussing method and marking a draft honestly. Writing, rewriting or supplying data for an Internal Assessment, Extended Essay, TOK essay or IGCSE coursework would breach academic integrity rules, so it is not something our tutors do." },
    { question: "Which IB Diploma subjects can you support for a Simdega student?", answer: "Most of the subject groups: both Mathematics courses, the three sciences, Environmental Systems and Societies, Geography, Economics, Business Management, English A, Hindi B, Computer Science, Psychology and Sports, Exercise and Health Science, plus Theory of Knowledge and the Extended Essay process. Tell us the exact subject and level when you write, since that decides whether we can match someone who has taught it recently." },
    { question: "Do you tutor MYP and PYP students linked to Simdega, not only the Diploma?", answer: "Yes, the whole continuum is covered. MYP help usually concerns criterion-based work, the Personal Project journal and reasoning in science or mathematics, while PYP help is shorter and gentler, built around reading, number sense and preparing for the Exhibition. With no local IB school, these students are most often in a boarding school or have moved with a parent's posting." },
    { question: "Is online tutoring as effective as lessons in a room for IB or IGCSE?", answer: "For syllabus-specific teaching it usually matches a classroom session, because the valuable part is a tutor's knowledge of the course and quick marking, not shared air. A whiteboard, a past paper worked through live and a recap saved for revision cover most needs. Where a Simdega student has no local specialist at all, online is the only route to that knowledge." },
    { question: "How are IB Gram tutors vetted for Simdega students?", answer: "Before a name reaches a family, we check qualifications, recent teaching of the specific subject and level, and how the tutor handles Internal Assessment guidance within academic integrity rules. For a place like Simdega, with no local school to sanity-check against, recent hands-on experience of the syllabus is weighted heavily. You then judge the tutor yourself in the free trial lesson." },
    { question: "When should a Simdega student start IB or IGCSE tutoring?", answer: "At the start of the course if possible: Grade 9 for IGCSE and Class 11 for the Diploma. Early lessons fix foundations before internal exams, Internal Assessment deadlines and predicted grades arrive. A student who begins later still has real options, though the plan then narrows to the topics and paper skills that carry the most marks before the target session." },
    { question: "My child is moving from the Jharkhand board or CBSE to IB or IGCSE. Can a tutor help?", answer: "Yes, and it is among the most useful things a tutor can do. The content gap is usually smaller than the gap in expectations: command terms such as evaluate and justify, extended written answers, criteria-based marking and planned coursework. Starting in the summer before the move gives time to practise these on familiar content, so the new school's pace feels manageable." },
    { question: "Can lessons fit around hockey practice or a boarding school timetable?", answer: "Yes. A weekly slot is agreed around school hours, training and prep time, and it can be moved when a fixture list or hostel routine changes. Early evenings after practice and weekend mornings are common choices, and a boarder can use a free period the school allows. Tell the tutor about tournaments or camps early so that no lesson is missed." },
    { question: "What if the internet drops during a lesson in the rainy season?", answer: "Plan for it rather than hope: keep a second connection, such as a mobile hotspot on a different network, and tell the tutor if power cuts are common so timings can be adjusted. A short drop usually means a pause and a reconnect, and the tutor can send the remaining work in the written note. Testing the setup during the free trial lesson reveals most problems early." },
    { question: "Can IB or IGCSE tutoring run alongside NEET or JEE coaching?", answer: "Yes, but they are different tracks and should be planned as such. Subject tutoring stays inside the IB or IGCSE syllabus and its assessments, while entrance preparation follows the national exam syllabus. A student attempting both has to be realistic about hours, because a Diploma student with three HL subjects, TOK and CAS already has a full week." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram connected with any school, the IB or Cambridge?", answer: "No. IB Gram is an independent tutoring service with no partnership with, endorsement from or representation of any school named on this page, the International Baccalaureate, Cambridge International Education or Pearson. Schools appear only to help Simdega families understand where international curricula are taught." },
  ],

